# Refined proof target

The remaining theorem is now:

```text
The family-trivial residual CP labels (w,n) are the unitary characters dual
to the integral Lens x Nil component lattice generated by beta_1,beta_3,
and the coherent-projector descent preserves the primitive integer block
K=[[2,1],[1,4]].
```

Then:

```text
Gamma_7 ~= Hom(Lambda_beta / K Lambda_beta, U(1)) ~= Z_7.
```

Combining with the dyadic carry gives:

```text
Gamma_CP,min ~= Z_64 x Z_7 ~= Z_448.
```

Adding family gives the ambient carrier:

```text
Gamma_amb ~= Z_64 x Z_7 x Z_3 ~= Z_1344.
```

# Bottom line

We have moved the sevenfold problem from:

```text
find Z_7 somewhere.
```

to:

```text
prove a dual-lattice descent identification.
```

That is much sharper.  The algebra is now complete conditional on the descent
identification; the physical/topological work is to show that the CP Wilson/nil
labels are exactly the dual characters of the integral Lens x Nil component
lattice and that the integer block is exact.
